MinimalPrimes -- minimal primes and radical routines for ideals
***************************************************************

Description
===========

Find the *note minimal primes of an ideal: minimal primes of an ideal, in a
polynomial ring over a prime field, or a quotient ring of that. These are the
geometric components of the corresponding algebraic set.

Multiple strategies are implemented via *note hooks: (Macaulay2Doc)using
hooks,. In many cases the default Birational strategy is much faster, although
there are cases when the Legacy strategy does better. For a *note monomial
ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, a more efficient algorithm is used
instead.

minprimes and decompose are synonyms for *note minimalPrimes: minimalPrimes,.

Caveat
======

Only works for ideals in (commutative) polynomial rings or quotients of
polynomial rings over a prime field, might have bugs in small characteristic
and larger degree (although, many of these cases are caught correctly).

* Menu:

* minimalPrimes::               minimal primes of an ideal
* isPrime(Ideal): (Macaulay2Doc)isPrime_lpIdeal_rp.
* radical(Ideal): radical.      the radical of an ideal
* minimal primes of an ideal::
* radical of an ideal::

