isPrime(Ideal) -- whether an ideal is prime
*******************************************

  * Function: *note isPrime: (Macaulay2Doc)isPrime,
  * Usage: 
        isPrime I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, in a polynomial ring or
        quotient of one
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value null,
        See *note minimalPrimes(...,Strategy=>...): minimalPrimes,
      * Verbosity => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0, See
        *note minimalPrimes(...,Verbosity=>...): minimalPrimes,
      * SquarefreeFactorSize
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, *note true:
        (Macaulay2Doc)true, if I is a prime ideal, or *note false:
        (Macaulay2Doc)false, otherwise

Description
===========

This function determines whether an ideal in a polynomial ring is prime.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialCurveIdeal(R, {1, 5, 8})                             |
|                                                                      |
|               2    2      3    2 2   3     3    5        3   5    4  |
|o2 = ideal (a*c  - b d, b*c  - a d , b c - a d, c  - a*b*d , b  - a c)|
|                                                                      |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isPrime I                                                        |
|                                                                      |
|o3 = true                                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note minimalPrimes: minimalPrimes, -- minimal primes of an ideal

