radicalContainment -- whether an element is contained in the radical of an ideal
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        radicalContainment(g, I)
  * Inputs:
      * g, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => ..., default value "Rabinowitsch"
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if g is in the
        radical of I, and false otherwise

Description
===========

This method determines if a given element g is contained in the radical of a
given ideal I. There are 2 algorithms implemented for doing so: the first
(default) uses the Rabinowitsch trick in the proof of the Nullstellensatz, and
is called with Strategy => "Rabinowitsch". The second algorithm, for
homogeneous ideals, uses a theorem of Kollar to obtain an effective upper bound
on the required power to check containment, together with repeated squaring,
and is called with Strategy => "Kollar". The latter algorithm is generally
quite fast if a Grobner basis of I has already been computed. A recommended way
to do so is to check ordinary containment, i.e. g % I == 0, before calling this
function.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : d = (4,5,6,7)                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = (4, 5, 6, 7)                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : n = #d                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = 4                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : R = QQ[x_0..x_n]                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = ideal homogenize(matrix{{x_1^(d#0)} | apply(toList(1..n-2), i -> x_i|
|                                                                             |
|             4     5      4     6      5     7      6                        |
|o4 = ideal (x , - x  + x x , - x  + x x , - x  + x x )                       |
|             1     2    1 4     3    2 4     0    3 4                        |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|- x_(i+1)^(d#i)) | {x_(n-1) - x_0^(d#-1)}}, x_n)                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D = product(I_*/degree/sum)                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 840                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : x_0^(D-1) % I != 0 and x_0^D % I == 0                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : elapsedTime radicalContainment(x_0, I)                                  |
| -- .104651s elapsed                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : elapsedTime radicalContainment(x_0, I, Strategy => "Kollar")            |
| -- .00212085s elapsed                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : elapsedTime radicalContainment(x_n, I, Strategy => "Kollar")            |
| -- .00162828s elapsed                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

