radical of an ideal
*******************

There are two main ways to find the radical of an ideal. On some large examples
the second method is faster.

using *note radical: radical,
=============================

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[x,y,z]         |
|                               |
|o1 = S                         |
|                               |
|o1 : PolynomialRing            |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^3-y^2,y^2*z^2)|
|                               |
|             3    2   2 2      |
|o2 = ideal (x  - y , y z )     |
|                               |
|o2 : Ideal of S                |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : radical I                 |
|                               |
|                       3    2  |
|o3 = ideal (y*z, x*z, x  - y ) |
|                               |
